Walter D. Pullen wrote:
> Another non-food tin idea: A can of whoop ass! ;) When you open one, you
> get the YAFM of "You open a can of whoop ass". This idea isn't new, but for
> the next 20 turns or so all damage you deal to anything gets doubled. Great
> for when surrounded by a horde. If that's unbalancing, at least make it (or
> the can of worms message) a random hallucination message when opening a tin.

     I upgraded to Nethack 3.4.3 earlier today, and since I had the source out, 
I decided to try implementing a YANI for the first time, specifically the 
hallucination message (the whole "whoop ass" tin is too hard for me right now). 
It was pretty trivial (basically add a few lines to where the random monster is 
generated in opentin() in eat.c), but right now the tins that receive this 
message (or "can of worms") are silently discarded, regardless of what they are, 
after opening them (a risk of hallucinating, I guess).

     It would make more sense to have "can of whoop ass" when you open a can of 
spinach while hallucinating (because of the strength bonus), but then the 
"Swee'pee" message wouldn't make much sense. Unless...

You open up a can of whoop ass!
It smells like spinach. Eat it? y
This makes you feel like Swee'pea!

